WARDEN_USAGE=$(cat <<'USAGE'
\033[33mUsage:\033[0m
  account-reset-password --email <email>                         Sets a new password in the local D1 database
  account-reset-password -- --remote --email <email>             Does the same in the live Cloudflare D1 database

  The new password is typed hidden at the prompt (min 12 characters). It is never a command argument.
  The account's lockout is cleared and its sessions are signed out.
  Warden 0.16 rejects a bare --remote, so put -- before it.
  --remote needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID in .env, and asks you to type 'live' first.

\033[33mOptions:\033[0m
  -h, --help        Display this help menu
USAGE
)
